I also need a winter jacket.
I look at more clothes in the shop.
I find a beautiful, green coat.
It is a very beautiful design.
I put the green coat on.
But it is too small.
It is very tight across the shoulders.
"Do you have it in a large size?" I ask.
The shop assistant looks.
"No, unfortunately," she answers.
So I hang the green coat back.
The shop assistant finds another jacket for me.
It is a warm, dark-blue winter jacket.
I put the dark-blue jacket on.
It fits perfectly.
It is nice and big and not tight.
I look in a large mirror.
I like it.
"I will take it," I say.
